[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Its reports show separate
problems, counted below. The queued parser fix closes only `parser`.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. One ticket per problem. Fixing the parser leaves the others open.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

- **`parser`** — the shared parser reads every date month first. Day-first tenants get day and
  month swapped: 7 April becomes 4 July.
- **`hint`** — booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People at a day-first tenant
  type month first, as told, and the form reads it day first. Same symptom, different code: the
  parser fix does not reach it.
- **`one-day-move`** — the date moves by one day; nothing is swapped. "Client in Lisbon got
  Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday." The desk already read these as one-day moves
  (`desk-notes.json`) but files them under `parser` by tenant. They look like a time-zone or
  offset bug.

## How the reports were placed

The counts are the desk's own view, the same logic as the #4471 table below: each report counted
once by id (the export pages overlap, so some rows repeat), filed under its cause by tenant and
the way it came in (`causeOf` in `causes.ts`). The reports the desk read as a one-day move stay
filed under their cause and are counted again as their own problem. That logic is `problemsIn`
in `#lib/kb/problems.ts`, so the table above recomputes when the export changes.

Every report body was read against that placement: all but a handful show an exact day/month
swap, the one-day moves show a one-day shift, and the rest are too vague to place by body.

Intake's tag is no guide here: it guesses from the reporter's browser, not the tenant, so it
tags `hint` reports `parser` and `parser` reports `hint`. Both tables count by tenant.

## The same reports, as #4471 shows them

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

This is the table on the #4471 page. It already splits `hint` from `parser`, and footnotes the
one-day moves under `parser`.

## For the desk

- Close each problem on its own ticket. #4471 stays open until every problem is fixed.
- Merging on subject ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) put them all under
  one ticket: "Date is wrong" and "Month and day swapped?" come in under every problem.

